<title>GREECE: Tempest's emerging mkt survey on Greece.</title>
<headline>Tempest's emerging mkt survey on Greece.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek Sigma Securities, Alpha Brokerage, National Securities, N.D. Devletoglou Securities got high marks from fund managers and financial directors for research, sales and trading in Tempest's global emerging market survey.</p>
<p>Sigma Securities was ranked first by both fund managers and finance directors.</p>
<p>George Liaskas of Intertrust SA was voted among the best 10 fund managers by finance directors in the same survey.</p>
<p>FINANCE DIRECTOR RANKING OF TOP INDIVIDUAL FUND MANAGERS 1.</p>
<p>Mark Mobius of Templeton Investment Management 2. </p>
<p>Ian Preston of Liberty Asset Management 3.</p>
<p>Herman Van Velze of Standard Bank Asset management 4. </p>
<p>Kokkic Kooyman of Old Mutual </p>
<p>5. George Liaskas of Intertrust</p>
<p>Jack Mitchell  of AGIC</p>
<p>Colin Stone    of Fidelity Investments</p>
<p>GREECE-FUND MANAGERS RANKING (WEIGHTED)</p>
<p>1. Sigma Securities (Athina Dessypri, team)</p>
<p>2. ING Barings     (Ioannis Protopapadakis, team, David</p>
<p>							Straker-Smith)</p>
<p>3. Schroders	 (Stuart Harley, Melina Androutsopoulou)</p>
<p>4. Carnegie	  (Mariella Porfyratos)</p>
<p>5. Alpha Brokerage  (Dimitri Veriopoulos)</p>
<p>GREECE-FINANCE DIRECTORS RANKING (WEIGHTED)</p>
<p>1.  Sigma Securities 2.  Alpha Brokerage</p>
<p>3.  National Securities</p>
<p>4.  N.D. Devletoglou Securities</p>
<p>5.  ING Barings</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
